  "scope": "Certified w(r), w_r(r) polynomial packets for an exact finite-tail grid.\n\nAn approximate cubic inverse is only a proposal. Its true radial residual\nis enclosed by the validated source primitive, then multiplied by the\nreviewed global bound |w_r|<24. A direct forward-bracketed inverse box\nencloses w_r on outer profiles. Inner profiles may use the independent\nglobal cap and curvature bounds. No floating inverse is trusted as exact. Across cap boundaries w is C4;\nonly its order-four Taylor remainder is used there, even though the\nindividual branch expressions are not analytic across the boundary.\nA first-derivative residual enclosure preserves radius correlation even\nwhen the proposal crosses many tiny primitive leaves.\n",
